Use the following as engineering targets, not claims of current performance:

- Selection should feel immediate.
- Hover outlines should update smoothly.
- Expensive work must not block pointer interaction.
- Selection changes should avoid remounting heavy components.
- Overlay updates should aim to stay within the browser frame budget.

At 60Hz, one frame is approximately 16.67ms.

Use this as a reference when evaluating work performed during interactive frames.

Do not interpret the entire 16.67ms as available for the selection engine alone.

## 55. Avoid full-document updates

